.TH nvfwupd 1
.SH NAME
nvfwupd \- Out-of-Band Tool to update NVIDIA DGX, HGX, MGX platforms. 
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nvfwupd
[global options]
[command]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nvfwupd
This tool performs out-of-band firmware update of the entire DGX, HGX, MGX, PowerShelf, and switch platforms. It can also update an individual component of these platforms. For supported switch targets, it can display and install NVOS image versions. Additionally, it supports in-band operations for flint-based firmware queries and updates on the Host OS.
.PP
Redfish connections use HTTPS by default. Cleartext HTTP connections are disabled by default; use \fBallow_http=true\fR only for trusted HTTP-only Redfish targets or port-forwarding cases.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR "-t/--target < sub-options >"
Specify target platform BMC or NVOS IP address and login credentials.
.RS
.IP SUB-OPTIONS
<key=value> pairs of input parameters that describe the target machine.
.TP "ip=<value> user=<value> password=<value> port=<value> servertype=<value>"
.RS
.IP ip 0.20i
IP address/FQDN of target BMC or NVOS service.
.IP user
Username to login to the target BMC or NVOS service.
.IP password
Password to login to the target BMC or NVOS service.
.IP port
TCP port with port-forwarding to use to connect with BMC service (optional)
.IP servertype
Users can provide the servertype value from the [DGX | DGXRUBIN | HGX | MGX | GH200 | HGXB100 | HGXB300 | HGXRUBIN | GB200 | GB300 | VRNVL72 | LP30 | GB200Switch | GB300Switch | VRNVL72Switch | PowerShelf] options based on the type of the target system type. This is optional and is recommended only if you experience unknown platform errors.
.RE
.RE
.TP
.BR "-o/--os_target < sub-options >"
Specify target Host OS IP address and login credentials for in-band operations. 
.RS
.IP SUB-OPTIONS
<key=value> pairs of input parameters that describe the target Host OS.
.TP "ip=<value> user=<value> password=<value> port=<value> servertype=<value>"
.RS
.IP ip 0.20i
IP address/FQDN of target Host OS.
.IP user
Username to login to the target Host OS.
.IP password
Password to login to the target Host OS.
.IP port
SSH port number (optional).
.IP servertype
Server type (optional).
.RE
.RE
.TP
.BR "-c/--config < config YAML path >"
A YAML config file can be used to define the behavior of few commands. This option takes the path of such YAML config file (optional).
.TP
.BR "-v/--verbose < logfile path >"
Increase verbosity. Provide chosen path for logfile (optional). Default path is current working directory.
.SH COMMAND
.TP
.BR "show_version <command options>"
Show AP components that can be updated out-of-band along with current running firmware versions. If -p option is specified, then show firmware versions from the firmware package, firmware tar file, or supported switch NVOS .bin image, and whether each AP component is up-to-date or needs updating. Global option -t/--target required.
.IP "COMMAND OPTIONS"
.RS
.IP -p/--package 0.20i
PLDM firmware package, firmware tar file, or supported switch NVOS .bin image. (optional)
.IP -j/--json 0.20i
Display package comparison in JSON format. (optional)
.IP -s/--staged 0.20i
Display staged firmware versions. (optional)
.IP -i/--inventory 0.20i
Include Software Inventory in the output (e.g. IST test vector versions). Queries the Redfish UpdateService SoftwareInventory collection and displays version information in the same table as firmware inventory. (optional)
.RE
.TP
.BR "update_fw <command options>"
Perform firmware update of the entire server out-of-band using a PLDM package or firmware tarball. Supported switch targets also accept one NVOS .bin image. If -s option is specified, firmware update only the AP component(s) mentioned in the JSON file. Global option -t/--target required.
.IP "COMMAND OPTIONS"
.RS
.IP -p/--package 0.20i
PLDM firmware package, firmware tar file, or one supported switch NVOS .bin image (mandatory).
.IP -b/--background
Perform firmware update asynchronously in the background.
.IP -s/--special
Special Update json file.
.IP -o/--oem_parameters
Oem Parameters json file.
.IP -t/--timeout
API request timeout value in seconds. For NVOS .bin updates, this also controls SFTP upload timeout.
.IP -e/--expected_inventory
JSON file listing FirmwareInventory AP names that must be present before update. If omitted, expected inventory validation is skipped.
.IP -y/--yes
Bypass firmware update confirmation prompt.
.IP -d/--details
Show update progress in table format.
.IP -j/--json
Show output in JSON. Must be paired with the -b background option, and always bypasses update confirmation prompt.
.IP -u/--staged_update
Run a SPI staged update for components that support it. (optional)
.IP -a/--staged_activate_update
Run a SPI staged and activate update for components that support it. (optional)
.IP -k/--skip_pre_flight_checks
Skip pre-flight checks before firmware update, such as update task status, BackgroundCopy, and write-protect checks where supported. Use with caution. Can also be set in the YAML config file using SkipPreFlightChecks parameter. This option does not disable expected inventory validation when -e/--expected_inventory is provided. (optional)
.RE
.TP
.BR "activate_fw <command options>"
Perform firmware activation using IPMI commands . Global option -t/--target required.
.IP "COMMAND OPTIONS"
.RS
.IP -c/--cmd 0.20i
Activation command to run. Supported values ['PWR_STATUS', 'PWR_OFF', 'PWR_ON', 'PWR_CYCLE', 'RESET_COLD', 'RESET_WARM', 'NVUE_PWR_CYCLE', 'RF_AUX_PWR_CYCLE', 'RF_PWR_ON', 'RF_PWR_OFF', 'RF_PWR_CYCLE', 'RF_PWR_STATUS', 'RF_PWRSHELF_RESET', 'RF_PWRSHELF_RESET_FORCE'] (mandatory).
.RE
.TP
.BR "background_copy <command options>"
Initiate background copy of the component identified in JSON file given with -s. Global option -t/--target required.
.IP "COMMAND OPTIONS"
.RS
.IP -s/--special 0.20i
JSON file used to select the background copy target component. (mandatory)
.IP -i/--interactive
Interactive mode - poll until Active and Inactive firmware slots match
.IP -t/--timeout
Maximum wait time in seconds for interactive mode polling (default 600)
.IP -p/--poll_interval
Poll interval in seconds for interactive mode (default 20)
.RE
.TP
.BR "force_update <option_value> <command options>"
Command to check/enable/disable the force update flag on target system. Used for downgrades. Global option -t/--target required.
.IP "OPTION VALUE"
.RS
.IP enable 0.20i
Enable force update on target.
.IP disable
disable force update on target.
.IP status
Show status of force update on target.
.RE
.IP "COMMAND OPTIONS"
.RS
.IP -j/--json
show output in JSON
.RE
.TP
.BR "show_update_progress <command options>"
Show current status of an update task running on target. Global option -t/--target required.
.IP "COMMAND OPTIONS"
.RS
.IP -i/--id 0.20i
Task ID of the update task to monitor.
.IP -j/--json
show output in JSON
.RE
.TP
.BR "make_upd_targets <command options>"
Create all update parameter JSON files for given target. Global option -t/--target required.
.IP "COMMAND OPTIONS"
.RS
.IP -o/--outdir 0.20i
Path for output directory to store the JSON files (optional). Default location is current working directory. If given directory path does not exist, the tool will try to create it.
.RE
.TP
.BR "perform_factory_reset"
Perform factory reset on target system. This is not supported on the NVSwitch trays. Global option -t/--target required.
.TP
.BR "show_pkg_content <command options>"
Show PLDM metadata for all firmware devices in a fwpkg file. -p/--package is mandatory. Global options not required. 
.IP "COMMAND OPTIONS"
.RS
.IP -p/--package 0.20i
PLDM firmware package file. Not supported with tar files.
.RE
.TP
.BR "unpack <command options>"
Unpack all firmware images from a PLDM package and show associated metadata for all firmware devices. -p/--package is mandatory. Global options not required. 
.IP "COMMAND OPTIONS"
.RS
.IP -p/--package 0.20i
PLDM firmware package file. Not supported with tar files.
.IP -o/--outdir
Path for output directory to store the unpacked firmware files (optional). Default location of unpacked files is current working directory. If given directory path does not exist, the tool will try to create it.
.RE
.TP
.BR "flint_update <command options>"
Execute flint queries and firmware updates on the Host OS. This command connects to the target system's Host OS via SSH and performs flint-based firmware operations. Global option -o/--os_target required.
.IP "COMMAND OPTIONS"
.RS
.IP -i/--image 0.20i
Image file(s) for firmware flashing and version comparison. Can specify multiple image files.
.IP -d/--device_type
Device type for firmware flashing and version query (e.g., BlueField3, ConnectX).
.IP -j/--json
Show output in JSON format for automation and parsing.
.IP -v/--version
Query firmware version only without performing updates.
.IP -t/--timeout
Query timeout in seconds for OS commands. Flashing operation timeout is 20x the query timeout. (default 60 for queries, 1200 for flash operations) This can be set higher for slow networks.
.RE
